WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.450
Correlation and regression

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:10.110
What do the sign and size of r tell you?

3
00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:20.330
Sign is direction, size is strength, range −1 to +1. r = 0 means no straight-line relationship — a perfect U-shape has r near zero.

4
00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:23.960
What is r²?

5
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:35.970
The share of variation in Y that X accounts for. Chocolate and Nobels: r = 0.79, so r² ≈ 0.62 — impressive-sounding and still not causal.

6
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:40.040
The sentence to write about a slope?

7
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:49.250
“A one-unit increase in X is associated with a change of b units in Y” — holding the other variables constant, and never “causes” unless the design earns it.

8
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.370
How do you read a regression table?

9
00:00:53.370 --> 00:01:02.900
Each row is a variable. The coefficient b gives direction and size; the standard error beside it gives precision; asterisks or a p-column give significance.

10
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.860
Quick significance check on a regression table?

11
00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.620
If the coefficient is more than about twice its standard error, it is significant at p &lt; .05.

12
00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.000
Correlation and regression — 5 cards
